80fc6c7a1cd2e86750971966a0687e040f1fb5e04c95353f1d73f1b1b3cde3cb","event_uuid":"9636959a-539b-42db-9d6c-7fd8592a7ad3","position":{"commit_sha":"4c6c190b0354d2feb6d0791303e7f666416948a1","position":"1788053920546173833-9636959a-539b-42db-9d6c-7fd8592a7ad3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"08d4c67fddf806398f49cd8c331f397610e9687ecbc4b412d746227fd726c90e","event_uuid":"df006187-1293-4c08-b1b8-998a73498660","position":{"commit_sha":"8768671aab08f19ce82b0897dee24f591e506e30","position":"1788055115159143022-df006187-1293-4c08-b1b8-998a73498660"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"f307f4501787333e1b687b8d3a2422477c54e9191e77c60f58d0aabf8d99105c","event_uuid":"d617e4d2-61bf-4070-92e4-1367f28e81dc","position":{"commit_sha":"7cd7582aae3aed27023d449263052b23f106b342","position":"1788056475337811866-d617e4d2-61bf-4070-92e4-1367f28e81dc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788029193534685748,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f91c632a-126f-41fa-9342-12dae4e3410c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"96f3-af59-ba26-4159"},{"link_uuid":"df006187-1293-4c08-b1b8-998a73498660","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6439-0483-9bd5-47a8"},{"link_uuid":"d617e4d2-61bf-4070-92e4-1367f28e81dc","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"471f-3110-6566-4eac"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEvaluating a Pass-1 change on Sonnet when production runs Opus (or vice versa) confounds the measurement: prior work showed Sonnet degrades past ~3 criteria per turn while Opus is flat, so a delta could be the model, not the change. Two further hazards: the production model classes (`rebar.toml` `[llm.model_classes]`: frontier = `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8`, standard = `bedrock:…claude-sonnet-4-6`) carry an Anthropic-direct fallback, and `_intersect_capabilities` (`src/rebar/llm/runner_support.py`) collapses a mixed chain's `prompt_cache_style` to `none` whenever the chain's candidates disagree — which is why cache reads dropped to zero on 2026-08-12 and review cost roughly doubled. `PydanticAIRunner.run` (`src/rebar/llm/runner.py:457-459`) RE-DERIVES the fallback chain from the resolved model STRING on every call — `fallback_targets = fallback_targets_for(resolved, repo_root=cfg.repo_path)`, which loads `[llm.model_classes]` fresh from `cfg.repo_path` and matches the class whose primary equals `resolved` — so a caller cannot suppress the fallback merely by not constructing a fallback list itself; the only existing suppression (`no_chain = self._model_override is not None`, runner.py:458) fires solely for the offline test-double path, not for a live eval run using the real model.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/parity.py` as a standalone module in THIS ticket (`tier1.py`, `tier2.py`, and `report.py` do not exist yet — they are built by later tickets in this epic, `presolar-finable-binturong`/Tier-1, `peaceable-choppy-sapsucker`/Tier-2, and the report module bundled with the Tier-0 ticket `bouncy-peacockish-titmouse`; THIS ticket only builds and unit-tests `parity.py`'s functions in isolation, exposing the API those later tickets will import and call — it does not itself edit tier1.py/tier2.py/report.py, and it makes NO change to `runner.py` or any production config, which are out of scope here):\n\n- **Pinned targets, with a GENUINELY homogeneous chain**: `resolve_pinned_model(pass_name)` maps `pass_name` to a production model class via `PASS_MODEL_CLASS = {\"pass1\": \"frontier\", \"pass2\": \"standard\"}` (Pass 3/decide is deterministic, not in this map — an unmapped `pass_name` raises `ValueError`). It reads the REAL production config via `model_classes.load_class_slots()` + `resolve_class(name, slots)` to get the class's true primary `provider:model` (requiring it to start with `bedrock:`, refusing otherwise), THEN writes a small ephemeral `rebar.toml` into a fresh `tempfile.mkdtemp()` directory containing only `[llm.model_classes]` for that ONE class, with `model` copied from the real primary and `fallback = []` (empty — no Anthropic candidate to re-attach). It returns `PinnedModel(model_id: str, config_root: str)` — both the resolved Bedrock model id AND that temp directory's path. **Eval-run callers (the later Tier-1/Tier-2 tickets) MUST construct their `LLMConfig(repo_path=pinned.config_root)`** for that pass's call, so that `fallback_targets_for`'s lookup (keyed on `cfg.repo_path`, per `runner.py:457`) resolves against the fallback-free ephemeral config instead of the real `rebar.toml` — this is the actual, confirmed mechanism that keeps the chain homogeneous, not merely \"the caller doesn't build a list.\" `check_model_parity(pass_name, resolved_id, baseline_ran_model)` refuses when `resolved_id` differs from a supplied baseline `ran_model` for that pass, unless `allow_model_change=True` is passed, in which case the result is labelled `model-change`.\n- **Result stamping helper**: `stamp_pass_model(result, pass_name, model_id)` and `refuse_diff_on_model_mismatch(result_a, result_b)` — the latter raises when two result dicts carry different per-pass model ids under a `models: {pass: model_id}` key. (Later tickets call this from `report.py`, which does not exist yet.)\n- **Caching check**: `check_cache_effective(usage_rows)` asserts from a list of usage-log row dicts that `cache_read_tokens > 0` on at least one row after the first, returning a `{\"cached\": bool, \"first_cache_hit_row\": int | None}` verdict callers can fold into a report or the ledger. (Later tickets call this after a live run and fold the verdict into the report/ledger — those integrations don't exist yet.)\n- No production config is changed by this ticket: the ephemeral fallback-free `rebar.toml` is written to a throwaway temp directory per pinned pass, never to the real repo root.\n\n**Corpus field addition needed by this ticket's own tests and by later parity checks**: `corpus.py`'s `_build_sidecar_row` (`src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py`) currently emits a row with `verdict`/`material_fingerprint`/etc. but does not surface `provider_provenance.ran_model` from the sidecar's `data` dict. Add a `ran_model` key to the emitted row (`data.get(\"provider_provenance\", {}).get(\"ran_model\")`, `None` when absent). This is additive to the row SHAPE but IS a material content change: `_compute_manifest` hashes every key of every row, so adding `ran_model` changes `content_hash` for every future corpus build — the already-committed `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/corpus-2026-08-29.manifest.json` becomes stale and must be regenerated and re-committed as part of this ticket's own integration step.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/parity.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py` (edit: add `ran_model` to the sidecar row)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/corpus-<date>.manifest.json` (regenerated: new content_hash from the added row field)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_parity.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: `resolve_pinned_model(\"pass1\")`/`(\"pass2\")` resolve the frontier/standard Bedrock ids and return a `config_root` whose written `rebar.toml` has `fallback = []` for that class while `model` matches the real production primary; `load_class_slots(repo_root=that_config_root)` on the returned root proves the fallback is empty (a real, executable check of the mechanism, not just an assertion on the return value's shape). An unmapped pass_name raises `ValueError`; a config whose frontier class resolves to a non-Bedrock primary is refused. `refuse_diff_on_model_mismatch` raises on differing per-pass model ids and accepts identical ones. `check_cache_effective` marks a usage-log fixture with zero cache reads as uncached and one with `cache_read_tokens > 0` on a later row as cached. A corpus row built from a sidecar carrying `provider_provenance.ran_model` surfaces it as `ran_model`; one without the key surfaces `ran_model: None`. Live check (cache effectiveness against a real run using `pinned.config_root`) happens as part of the Tier-1 reproduction run in a later ticket, not here.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `resolve_pinned_model` maps `pass1`/`pass2` to the frontier/standard Bedrock ids and returns a `config_root` whose `rebar.toml` has an empty fallback for that class (verified by loading slots from that root), and refuses a resolved primary that is not a Bedrock id; checked by unit tests.\n- [ ] `refuse_diff_on_model_mismatch` raises when two result dicts carry differing per-pass model ids and accepts identical ones; checked by a unit test.\n- [ ] `check_cache_effective` correctly classifies a cached vs. an uncached usage-row fixture; checked by a unit test.\n- [ ] `corpus.py`'s sidecar row surfaces `ran_model` from `provider_provenance.ran_model`, absent-safe; the corpus manifest is regenerated so its `content_hash` reflects the new field; checked by a unit test and by re-running the corpus build.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`.\n- [ ] No LLM calls; checked by running with no provider credentials.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/parity.py","reason":"model-parity guard + homogeneous chain"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_parity.py","reason":"unit tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","759e-7dc1-675c-4877"],["relates_to","471f-3110-6566-4eac"],["relates_to","6439-0483-9bd5-47a8"],["relates_to","96f3-af59-ba26-4159"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","parent_status_uuid":"a089c8ad-fb66-4d75-9200-516ba1563e3d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["plan-review","evals","bedrock","model-parity"],"ticket_id":"efd4-847d-f7ad-47bc","ticket_type":"story","title":"Model-parity guard: pin each eval pass to its production model on a homogeneous Bedrock chain; confirm prompt caching","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["10499e46-9a35-49af-a69f-addd70bca7a2","84610e82-06e1-41f8-8da1-bac6d0df2c18","1189b665-cdbb-4476-bfbb-f21c764d3f05","2526f690-1bcc-45c6-9efb-6b97bb50fbca","ad938c80-c73e-4af3-98ab-28e5ff3692df","3d823fd8-b931-41dd-b6f1-59aa620941e3","ef45a029-b134-4999-8296-809aa0ed9482","a089c8ad-fb66-4d75-9200-516ba1563e3d","9636959a-539b-42db-9d6c-7fd8592a7ad3","df006187-1293-4c08-b1b8-998a73498660","d617e4d2-61bf-4070-92e4-1367f28e81dc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788056475337811867,"uuid":"7f8db2c1-8caf-4fef-834a-02f157885221"}